      "side": 1,
      "message": "For GPIOs, there is a dependency on case for at least the firmware_ECUsbPorts test.  This test uses the \"custom_usb_enable_pins\" property to construct s \"gpioget\" and \"gpioset\" command.  The cros-ec command parsing is case-insensitive, however the Zephyr shell is case sensitive.\n\nI think it would a nice config option to add to Zephyr to allow the shell to ignore case.\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/fw-testing-configs/+/refs/heads/main/volteer.json#25",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 20,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "49ec0de53278d3282bd3dd5e83bb1f7dc5b228fd",
