      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T16:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Zephyr shell should be fine, it\u0027s just passing the argument to find_signal_by_name, which is case insensitive, so you can use either as first argument to \"gpioget\" and \"gpioset\". The output of \"gpioget\" would change though and I see these two bits of code parsing it:\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/labpack/+/refs/heads/main/server/site_tests/firmware_ECUsbPorts/firmware_ECUsbPorts.py#84\n\nhttps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/tast-tests/+/refs/heads/main/src/chromiumos/tast/remote/bundles/cros/firmware/ec_usb_ports.go#159\n\nI can make those two regexp match case insensitive.\n\nFound some other references to cr50 and c2d2 code around the repository but I guess those are out of scope for now.",
