      "writtenOn": "2021-12-21T23:43:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about using DEVICE_DT_NAME() here instead? This would allow someone to use the label property to override the display name if they wanted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "49ec0de53278d3282bd3dd5e83bb1f7dc5b228fd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "947a652f_d4f0ef64",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T16:55:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking about aiming at removing the label property entirely from the binding. Do you think we may need an override? Ultimately we should be able to get the correct enum from a devicetree phandle. Another thing is that if we use DT_NODE_FULL_NAME, it would instantly change to all the boards without having to touch the individual gpio.dts files. Thinking it may be easier to find if something breaks, and then it\u0027s a small patch to revert.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "095c22f0_c717aa89",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "49ec0de53278d3282bd3dd5e83bb1f7dc5b228fd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b334325_c5554469",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 38,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-22T18:21:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Upstream I only see the tests using DT_NODE_FULL_NAME() and there looks to be a single user of DEVICE_DT_NAME() in the i2c.h API.\n\nI don\u0027t think you can actually eliminate the label property, since it is part of base.yaml.\n\nThere\u0027s probably no use case for overriding the node-full-name with a label.  So I\u0027m OK with DT_NODE_FULL_NAME().",
      "parentUuid": "947a652f_d4f0ef64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "49ec0de53278d3282bd3dd5e83bb1f7dc5b228fd",
